# Line endings: FREEZE what is committed. Do not renormalize.
#
# Settled in U1 of the v0.5 mechanistic-integration plan (T-K). The repository
# had no .gitattributes and no core.autocrlf, so every blob has been stored
# exactly as written. Of 133 tracked .tsv files: 61 are CRLF and 72 are LF, and
# none is mixed. `context/literature/pdf_manifest.tsv` was the one mixed file and
# was normalised to CRLF on 2026-09-18 by the unit that appended to it, which is
# what the note below asks a unit with a substantive reason to do.
#
# tests/unit/test_line_endings.py is authoritative for those figures, not this
# comment. An earlier revision of it said 46 CRLF -- the count before the same
# commit added the 14 CRLF tables under
# models/superset/adoc-literature-superset-v0.5.0/ -- which left a reader
# reconciling 46 here against 60 in PINNED_CRLF_BY_DIRECTORY with no way to tell
# which was current. If the two ever disagree again, the test is right.
# See docs/v05_line_endings.md for the reasoning.
#
# The obvious fix -- `*.tsv text eol=lf` -- is WRONG here and must not be added.
# Two of the four artifacts pinned to the frozen scRNA evidence root 91f79ed are
# CRLF (docs/scrna/node_support_evidence.tsv, 1429 lines;
# docs/scrna/node_rna_interpretability.tsv, 28 lines), as is
# docs/scrna/node_support_qc.tsv. Declaring eol=lf rewrites those blobs on the
# next checkout, which silently breaks the digests T-G exists to enforce -- and
# it does so without appearing in any commit diff, because the change happens at
# checkout rather than at edit. Provenance is not a formatting preference.
#
# `-text` means: never convert, in either direction, in any working tree. Bytes
# in the index are the bytes on disk. That is what keeps the freeze honest, and
# it is what tests/unit/test_line_endings.py asserts.
* -text

# Binary types, declared so git does not attempt textual diffs or merges on
# them. This changes presentation only; -text above already prevents conversion.
# data/ is immutable source evidence (docs/AGENTS.md) and is protected here without
# being modified: one tracked PDF contains byte sequences that a text-mode
# checkout on another platform could otherwise mangle.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.gif   binary
*.docx  binary
*.xlsx  binary
